# Scaffold-owned paths are authored with LF. Pin them so a checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) can never rewrite the
# bash scripts to CRLF — under Git Bash/MSYS a CRLF shebang script dies
# with "$'\r': command not found". Pinning also silences the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning flood while the installer stages.
#
# Trade-off: .github/** covers files YOU add there too (workflows, docs);
# LF is safe for YAML, Markdown, and shell. This file is seeded — it is
# yours after install — so extend or adjust the rules as your app needs.
.github/** text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
README.md text eol=lf
SCAFFOLD-CHANGELOG.md text eol=lf
